019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,69,2075,15087,387,264,729,1741,429,369,678,400,87,4779,400,69,2075,8,284,282,2075,488,220,16,8,488,282,2075,481,220,16,568,3,220,16246,429,400,69,7,16,20,8,284,220,17,15,3,323,400,69,7,17,15,8,284,220,16,20,4779,12564,400,69,7,17,15,16,20,17,15,16,20,568,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $f(x)$ be a function such that for all $x,$ $f(x) = f(x + 1) + f(x - 1).$  Given that $f(15) = 20$ and $f(20) = 15,$ compute $f(20152015).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"3a06947d31691cba40d873bfa71381aed6cb94523de23cfa4a624a1607c9fd49"},"seconds":27.373932600021362,"seed":894644712079974275,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we start by analyzing the given functional equation \\( f(x) = f(x+1) + f(x-1) \\). Let's define \\( a_n = f(n) \\). Then the equation can be rewritten as:\n\\[ a_n = a_{n+1} + a_{n-1}. \\]\nThis is a second-order linear homogeneous recurrence relation. To find a general solution, we assume \\( a_n = r^n \\). Substituting \\( a_n = r^n \\) into the recurrence relation, we get:\n\\[ r^n = r^{n+1} + r^{n-1}, \\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[ r^2 = r + 1. \\]\nThe solutions to this quadratic equation are:\n\\[ r = \\frac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}{2}. \\]\nLet \\( \\alpha = \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\) and \\( \\beta = \\frac{1 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\). The general solution to the recurrence relation is:\n\\[ a_n = A \\alpha^n + B \\beta^n, \\]\nwhere \\( A \\) and \\( B \\) are constants to be determined from the initial conditions.\n\nWe are given \\( a_{15} = 20 \\) and \\( a_{20} = 15 \\). Therefore, we have the system of equations:\n\\[ A \\alpha^{15} + B \\beta^{15} = 20, \\]\n\\[ A \\alpha^{20} + B \\beta^{15} = 15. \\]\n\nTo find a pattern, let's consider the values of \\( \\alpha \\) and \\( \\beta \\) more closely. Note that \\( \\beta = \\frac{1 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\) is a negative number less than -1, and \\( \\alpha = \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\) is a positive number greater than 1. As \\( n \\) becomes large, \\( \\alpha^n \\) grows exponentially, while \\( \\beta^n \\) approaches 0. Therefore, for large \\( n \\), the term \\( A \\alpha^n \\) will dominate the expression \\( A \\alpha^n + B \\beta^n \\).\n\nGiven that \\( \\alpha \\) and \\( \\beta \\) are roots of the characteristic equation, we can infer that the sequence \\( a_n \\) is periodic with a period that is a divisor of the minimal period of the recurrence relation. To find the period, we can check the values of \\( a_n \\) for small \\( n \\) and see if a pattern emerges.\n\nBy calculating the first few terms, we can observe:\n\\[ a_1 = f(1), \\]\n\\[ a_2 = f(2) = f(3) - f(1) = a_3 - a_1, \\]\n\\[ a_3 = f(3) = f(4) + f(2) = a_4 + a_2, \\]\n\\[ a_4 = f(4) = f(5) + f(3) = a_5 + a_3, \\]\nand so on. By solving these, we can find that the sequence is periodic with period 6. Therefore, \\( a_n = a_{n+6} \\).\n\nSince 20152015 mod 6 = 3, we have:\n\\[ a_{20152015} = a_3. \\]\nFrom the given values, we can find:\n\\[ a_{15} = 20, \\]\n\\[ a_{16} = a_{15} - a_{14} = a_{15} - (a_{15} - a_{13}) = a_{13}, \\]\n\\[ a_{17} = a_{16} - a_{15} = a_{13} - 20, \\]\n\\[ a_{18} = a_{17} - a_{16} = (a_{13} - 20) - a_{13} = -20, \\]\n\\[ a_{19} = a_{18} - a_{17} = -20 - (a_{13} - 20) = -a_{13}, \\]\n\\[ a_{20} = a_{19} - a_{18} = -a_{13} - (-20) = 20 - a_{13}. \\]\nSince \\( a_{20} = 15 \\), we have:\n\\[ 20 - a_{13} = 15, \\]\n\\[ a_{13} = 5. \\]\nTherefore, \\( a_3 = a_{15} - a_{14} = 20 - (20 - 5) = 5 \\).\n\nThus, the value of \\( f(20152015) \\) is \\( \\boxed{5} \\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{5}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:869"}
